Non-destructive disassembly for remanufacturing is characterised by: the preservation of all components in a reusable state; the use of reversible fasteners (screws, clips, snap-fits) rather than permanent joints (welds, adhesives); a defined disassembly sequence that minimises time and tool changes; compatibility with both manual and automated disassembly processes; and the ability to repeatedly disassemble and reassemble without degradation of joints or interfaces.